From: burakgon <burakgon12@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: dmi-quirks: Disable ghost rt722 on ASUS ExpertBook B9406CAA

The 2026 ASUS ExpertBook Ultra B9406CAA (Panther Lake, PCI audio subsystem
0x1043:0x15e4) advertises a phantom Realtek rt722 on SoundWire link 3
(_ADR 0x000330025d072201, status UNATTACHED) next to the real Cirrus
CS42L43. Both expose a JACK playback DAI, so the function-topology card
builder in sof_sdw creates two DAI links with the byte-identical name
"SDW3-Playback-SimpleJack":

  sysfs: cannot create duplicate filename '.../sof_sdw/SDW3-Playback-SimpleJack'
  kobject_add_internal failed for SDW3-Playback-SimpleJack with -EEXIST
  sof_sdw sof_sdw: probe with driver sof_sdw failed with error -12

The card never registers (empty /proc/asound/cards) and there is no audio.
On 7.0.x the static topology path did not trip on the ghost; the 7.1
function-topology builder does, because it builds the card from the
ACPI-declared functions.

This is the exact failure mode a5bec626b985 ("soundwire: dmi-quirks:
Disable ghost Realtek devices") addresses. The ghost's _ADR is identical
to the one already remapped for the ASUS UX5406AA and the two Lenovo
models, so reuse the existing ghost_realtek adr_remap and only add the
B9406CAA DMI match.

Tested on:
  - ASUS ExpertBook Ultra B9406CAA (Panther Lake, Core Ultra X7 358H)
  - Linux 7.1.x (CachyOS) with linux-firmware-cirrus providing the
    per-OEM cs35l56-b0-dsp1-misc-104315e4-l2u{0,1}.{wmfw,bin}

After the remap the ghost is skipped in drivers/soundwire/slave.c
(if (!addr) return false), leaving a single SDW3 jack; sof_sdw then
probes cleanly and all six speakers plus the headphone jack come up
through the standard HiFi UCM path.

Signed-off-by: burakgon <burakgon12@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/dmi-quirks.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/dmi-quirks.c b/drivers/soundwire/dmi-quirks.c
--- a/drivers/soundwire/dmi-quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/dmi-quirks.c
@@ -185,6 +185,13 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id adr_remap_quirk_table[] = {
 		},
 		.driver_data = (void *)ghost_realtek,
 	},
+	{
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "ASUS"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "B9406CAA"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = (void *)ghost_realtek,
+	},
 	{
 		.matches = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "LENOVO"),
